.TH CVECTOR_DATA_PTR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_data_ptr \- get pointer to internal data array
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

void *cvector_data_ptr(cvec v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a pointer to the vector's internal contiguous data array, which is
handy for passing the data to C APIs that expect an array.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to get the data pointer from
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the internal data array.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The pointer becomes invalid once the vector is resized. It points at
capacity elements, but only elem_count of them are valid. The function
asserts if v is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_data_ptr (3),
.BR cvector_at (3)
